ect a new momentum  into these negotiations that's our hope  and that's our commitment  my turn to a  rather different challenge uh to the eu  and foreign uh affairs and that is of  course  the fact that dozens of protesters and  12 police officers at least we think  have died in  ongoing violence in kazakhstan  russia has sent troops across the border  um  how worried is the eu about russian  incursion into its neighbors  well it's good that you mentioned russia  is good that you mentioned situation in  in kazakhstan because this is one area  of security in our neighborhood this is  one area where the eu and uk can do a  lot together and my my sense in looking  at the wider picture is that the sooner  we move on  from uh you know  issues that are still open related to  brexit in particular the north atlantic  situation the sooner we move on from  that  uh the better equipped we will be  the eu and the uk to work together in  addressing very serious issues uh  what can you do mr putin is not um  mr putin  doesn't do much uh uh responding to warm  words does he i mean what can you  actually do to stop well i think i think  i think  uh you know i was in liverpool in the in  the g7 foreign affairs ministers chaired  by by lee strauss and uh we together  agreed a very strong uh statement uh the  european union member states have a very  common position of strength the united  states is together the nato allies are  together and we are saying very clearly  uh and these are very clear words that  there will be massive consequences and  severe cost if russia  adventures into into ukraine with  military action and this is a very very  solid and unified position among  ourselves as you know today tomorrow the  days after there will be important  diplomatic  initiatives taking place i forgive you  too interrupting the  massive consequences that's that's a  good phrase would one massive  consequence be for the eu to say to mr  putin  if you keep on like this you can forget  about nordstream 2 and that flow of  revenue from oil and gas into western  europe i don't think we should  anticipate action  we should react when action takes place  what we're doing now is trying to  de-escalate using all the diplomatic  tools and avenues that are available if  ever  russia  moves into other direction they can be  sure that there will be a unified  response from our side and let me give  you this also as an example of the need  for us to move on in our bilateral  relationship because we are we share the  same values we share the same strategic  interests and there's a lot we need to  do regarding our neighborhood but also  regarding iran where we have a very  clear joint position with uk our  relationship with other parts of the  world thank you and the cooperation with  the us so it's a long list  and that is awaiting a better climate  thank you ambassador thank you so much
 

